A defining gesture of ‘In Minor Keys’ — the central exhibition of the 61st Venice Biennale curated by the late Koyo Kouoh — is the integration of six artist-led organisations who form its Schools. They function simultaneously as subject, methodology, and forms of knowledge production, resisting market imperatives and national categorisation.⁠
⁠
Browse our installation views of the four Africa-based Schools via link in @contemporaryand bio. ⁠
